zha lu dgon pa'i dpe mdzod<persName ref="person:5835" role="owner">chos skyong dpal ldan</persName>
                  </provenance>
               </history>
               <additional>
                  <adminInfo>
                     <availability>
                        <p>available</p>
                     </availability>
                     <note type="comment">Blurred seal on the cover page and annotation 5(80), as well as the indication that fol. 19 is missing - all of those likely from the library that preserved the manuscript. &#13;
No signature is visible on the reproduction, but [6TNNKSQ3]: 66 reports the 'Bras spungs gnas bcu lha khang signature phyi tsa 62 and indicates that the manuscript is now preserved at the library of Zha lu monastery.&#13;
&#13;
After the colophon, in the same handwriting, one finds the mention of the owner, a lineage ending with the author's successor Phyogs las rnam rgyal (ID:4214), and a verse by the scribe.</note>
                  </adminInfo>
